content:
sophia: Heads-up: StackBridge onboarding demo shows a reproducible 429 spike on init. Their dashboard opens several embedded webviews and a worker; all call sdk.init() immediately. Failures start ~8-20s into the demo.

sophia: demo logs:
```
[2026-04-18T13:08:41Z] webview-1 init /v1/preflight 200
[2026-04-18T13:08:42Z] webview-2 init /v1/preflight 429 x 10
[2026-04-18T13:08:42Z] sw init /v1/preflight 429 x 6
[2026-04-18T13:08:43Z] worker telemetry /v1/preflight 429 x 9
```

aar: Which SDK + auth? Are they using a single server key distributed into the installer?

sophia: Browser SDK v1.8.4 in embedded webviews, and yes — they used a shared dev key in the demo build to simplify onboarding. No client-side splay or inflight guard.

rachel: Classic init cookoff. Immediate advice for the customer: 1) switch to ephemeral session tokens per-view, 2) defer non-essential inits until user interaction, 3) add randomized init jitter and an inflight guard per-origin. Minimal jitter snippet to send them:```js
// jittered init + single inflight guard
if (window.__SB_init) return;
const delay = 200 + Math.floor(Math.random()*800); // 200-1000ms
setTimeout(()=>{
  if (window.__SB_init) return;
  window.__SB_init = true;
  sdk.init().finally(()=> window.__SB_init = false);
}, delay);
```

aar: Also recommend a tiny mint endpoint on their backend to issue 60s tokens. If they can't flip quickly, give them a simple coalescing proxy snippet:```js
let pendingMint=null;
async function mintToken(){
  if (pendingMint) return pendingMint;
  pendingMint = fetch('/internal/mint',{method:'POST'}).then(r=>r.json()).finally(()=> pendingMint=null);
  return pendingMint;
}
```

rachel: Ops-side quick fixes we can apply now: enable tenant preflight_coalesce for "stackbridge", temporarily increase burst_window by +180 tokens for 1h, and add a 2s leaky-bucket smoothing window on /v1/preflight for that tenant. That should blunt the immediate 429s while they roll ephemeral tokens.

rl-bot: RateLimitMonitor: tenant="stackbridge" detected 429 surge 2026-04-18T13:08:40Z..2026-04-18T13:12:00Z peak_preflight=172 req/min. Suggested actions: preflight_coalesce=true, burst_window_inc=+180, preflight_leaky_window=2000ms.

aar: I'll file an infra change request with TTL=60m for the burst bump + coalesce flag. Sophia, confirm the customer can roll ephemeral tokens in the maintenance window?

sophia: They can do a 30-min window starting in ~45 minutes. They'll accept the ops patch short-term. I'll share the jitter + mint snippets and schedule the window with the SE.

rachel: Post-rollout checklist: 1) monitor 429s for 2 hours, 2) sample 8 init traces across views, 3) sample 6 mint traces and confirm token variance per view, 4) verify latency and error budget. If 429s persist after client jitter + ephemeral tokens + coalesce, escalate to runtime for deeper KV-cache/coalescing and batching analysis.

sophia: Thanks — updating the onboarding ticket and looping infra/SE. Will post when the maintenance window is set. :thumbsup:
